Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: ONE transparent RTS infantry animation atlas. Reference image is APPROVED character and sixteen-heading contact sheet. Match its MODERATE detail, white/light gray uniform, steel helmet, brown belt and pouches, dark boots, wood-stock long rifle, adult proportions and restrained painted shading. Do not revert to the earlier cartoon/chibi simplification. Keep clear collar, a few purposeful folds, helmet brim, simple hands and rifle mechanism. No backpack or insignia.
Create exactly 4 ROWS by 5 COLUMNS, twenty separate full-body sprites in identical equal cells, generous empty gutters and no overlap or cropping. FIXED orthographic elevated camera 45 degrees above ground in EVERY cell. This atlas covers FOUR adjacent headings; each ROW has ONE unchanging heading:
row1 S / toward viewer; row2 SSW / 22.5° clockwise from front; row3 SW / 45° clockwise from front; row4 WSW / 67.5° clockwise from front.
These headings differ by exactly 22.5° around the upright axis, and must show visibly distinct body/helmet/face/rifle projections. In each row column 1 is STANDING READY matching that heading in reference. Columns 2 through 5 are FOUR successive RUN CYCLE poses at that exact same heading:
column2 left boot forward at ground contact, right leg trailing;
column3 passing pose, right knee drives forward and left boot below torso;
column4 right boot forward at ground contact, left leg trailing;
column5 passing pose, left knee drives forward and right boot below torso.
Running poses must have clear alternating legs, bent knees, modest forward lean and small natural torso bob, not standing poses with just a rifle change. Keep the helmet/body proportions, body center, equipment, light and size stable within each row. Rifle is supported firmly in BOTH hands and points ahead along the row's facing direction, slightly lower than firing aim while running. Right hand on stock, left hand under fore-end; preserve grip/shoulder across poses. Do not rotate camera or change direction across columns. Loop columns2,3,4,5 seamlessly. Fixed shared ground reference beneath the torso in all cells; running boots may lift but do not move whole character randomly within cells. Complete helmet, barrel, hands, legs and boots must fit in every cell with wide safe margins. Moderate hand-painted RTS sprite detail exactly like approved reference, not photoreal, not noisy, not pixelated, not chibi. TRUE TRANSPARENT background. No shadows baked into images, no terrain or floor, no labels/text, no grid, no UI, no smoke, no motion lines.

